{"summary":"Accept all six amendments. They identify real robustness and maintainability issues in the harness and validation layers, with the strongest concerns being silent NaN handling, runtime invariant repair that fabricates biological state, and artifact-path collisions across tests.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-32fa1988","decision":"accept","rationale":"The current NO3 windows in the moderate-water scenarios are effectively pinned to the 5.0 mg N/L source-water preset rather than the broader biological behavior the envelopes are supposed to preserve. That makes the tests brittle to legitimate kinetics and uptake retuning, while wider bounds plus explicit source-water documentation would still catch real regressions."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-423a179e","decision":"accept","rationale":"Envelope::check relies on plain floating-point comparisons, so NaN values bypass every bound check, and open-ended bounds such as do_min can also let +Inf slip through. Adding per-field finite checks at checkpoint time is a real correctness improvement because it surfaces bad states where they first appear instead of only at end-of-run."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-3081f78c","decision":"accept","rationale":"This test currently exercises a controlled best-case reproduction path, not a natural maintained-tank pathway, because it seeds reserve/readiness/periphyton and disables mortality. Calling that out explicitly is important for maintainability, and a companion test with much less state manipulation would restore coverage of actual maintained-tank survival behavior."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-fe5ff040","decision":"accept","rationale":"Runtime invariant enforcement should not synthesize new egg cohorts. Because enforce_invariants runs before and after step_hours, the current repair path can silently mutate live simulation outcomes, hide bookkeeping bugs, and even create near-hatching clutches that were never produced by the model. That repair belongs at load/migration boundaries, or the mismatch should fail fast."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7371c682","decision":"accept","rationale":"The artifact directory key is only scenario_id plus seed, but the suite now has multiple medium_planted runs with seed 42, including a from_state variant still labeled medium_planted. That creates a real collision/ambiguity bug for failure artifacts, especially under parallel execution, so an explicit per-run label in the path and metadata is warranted."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-2d8bb6d0","decision":"accept","rationale":"As written, the reproduction test is not a baseline guardrail for scenario behavior because it depends on hidden-state boosts and mortality being turned off. A named public fixture or scenario with normal mortality semantics is the correct shape for a real regression test against survival and stress behavior; otherwise this test can keep passing after those systems break."}]}